// An end-to-end spec finds a feed line by what happened and whose it is -
// `data-feed-event` and `data-feed-key`, through `reportLine` and its
// siblings in tests/e2e/rails.ts - or, for a line no task wrote, by the
// words its writer composes, imported (`feedLineOf(page, event)`, an
// action's `done` words, a composer called with the spec's own data),
// never by words typed into the spec (docs/testing.md, "The e2e assertion
// contract"). A feed line's sentence is its writer's to change and its unit
// tests' to pin (`feed.test.ts`, `taskFeed.test.ts`): every rewording broke
// the specs that re-typed it. So this rule refuses a string, a template or
// a regular expression - or a `new RegExp` built from one - as the text a
// spec hands `feedLine`. Runs inside `pnpm check` through biome.json's
// plugins, as an error since every spec moved.

language js

`feedLine($page, $text)` where {
  $text <: or {
    JsStringLiteralExpression(),
    JsTemplateExpression(),
    JsRegexLiteralExpression(),
    `new RegExp($source, $...)` where {
      $source <: or {
        JsStringLiteralExpression(),
        JsTemplateExpression()
      }
    }
  },
  $filename <: r".*tests/e2e/.*",
  register_diagnostic(span=$text, message="A feed line's composed words are its writer's to change and its unit tests' to pin. Find a task's line by its hooks - reportLine(page, key) and its siblings in tests/e2e/rails.ts - and a line no task wrote by its writer's own words, imported: feedLineOf(page, event), an action's done words or the composer called with this spec's data (docs/testing.md, the e2e assertion contract).", severity="error")
}
